      "created_at": "2018-02-21T17:48:55Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-02-21T17:48:55Z",
      "body": "This has been a subject of a lot of discussion in the Identity WG and other places.  Marta Piekarska is leading a collaborative effort to build out a paper on how Blockchains in general can address GDPR requirements here:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1wnRYOZrGZS6h_-PnJRaq1pAc35GrfGUZcXh46sTHdFQ/edit#heading=h.xlkpssu5kfbq\r\n\r\nCertainly we think that Indy's approach has many advantages when it comes to giving a user the ability to manage data sharing and meet GDPR requirements, but I am not aware of a paper that specifically addresses how Indy or an instance of Indy like Sovrin addresses GDPR requirements, but I could see how we could build out something very useful, and it would be a welcome contribution.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
